The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ A ], the reply is a fence containing only the object A, so the recovered object is A, and k_recovery returns the canonical JSON text of A. For the rewritten text fence[ A ] B, the fence now contains A and B. The recovery rule says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one. Since the fence holds A and B, the last object inside the fence is B, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON text of B. Therefore the answer moves between the two texts.